  "body": "## Status\nKourovka Notebook Problem 21.9 remains **unsolved after five substantive turns**. Full independent source/proof review passes all scoped results. No full resolution or historical novelty is claimed.\n\nThe packet establishes a p-adic abelianization obstruction, characteristic-core descent with an exact unresolved cofinality condition, all-depth commutator witnesses and their valuations, and a finite-rank normal-containment obstruction. Its abelian and Heisenberg comparison cases expose a finite-quotient lifting failure. **Those comparison groups are not nonabelian free pro-p groups and are not source counterexamples.**\n\n## Frozen evidence\n- All 36 author files and 5 independent-review files preserved\n- Final author WIP: 647033115e08e03872c5fcf01953a505b8ab2f0a\n- Author manifest SHA-256: d498046adc568031857dc5b93d7e8049a591f4f128f73666208fd8de0e4f0d8a\n- Review manifest SHA-256: 6ca9abdd890d5cead8ca8c5019396080121473b61867bb3654bf7ac4ea05b4a4\n- 139,300 author and 153,807 independent bounded exact assertions pass\n- Python standard library only; `python verify_publication.py` checks hashes and both replays\n\nThe original source is the October 2026 21st edition, printed 177. The September 22, 2026 primary commensurator paper repeats the exact question and distinguishes it from discrete free groups and finitely many individual automorphisms. Source PDFs/images remain local-only. The public replay explicitly omits the 12 raw source bindings while preserving their historical verified receipt.\n\n## Scope\nFresh-main integration preserves author ancestry. Only 44 target artifacts and this target's QUEUE status/turn cells change, to unsolved 5/5. No merge or release.\n\n[Reviewed status and replay instructions](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/fd4a71f2f7e08ece5f0d34d9d0df3fb6f460d8bf/problems/2518_free_pro_p_characteristic_intersections/REVIEWED_STATUS.md)",
